2. nvim-lspconfig — Apache-2.0, Neovim contributors
---------------------------------------------------

internal/gen/corpus/nvim-lspconfig/ holds a verbatim snapshot of six
server-configuration modules from nvim-lspconfig, written by the Neovim
contributors and distributed under the Apache License 2.0, reproduced in
full at internal/gen/corpus/nvim-lspconfig/LICENSE.md (copied verbatim
from the same commit). Upstream ships no NOTICE file, so Apache-2.0
section 4(d) imposes nothing further.

Provenance:

  github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig @ bff1bd61cb1455040533201ca1edf1e84efa578f
  (committed 2026-08-19T18:24:55Z)

    LICENSE.md            -> internal/gen/corpus/nvim-lspconfig/LICENSE.md
    lsp/clangd.lua        -> internal/gen/corpus/nvim-lspconfig/lsp/clangd.lua
    lsp/gopls.lua         -> internal/gen/corpus/nvim-lspconfig/lsp/gopls.lua
    lsp/lua_ls.lua        -> internal/gen/corpus/nvim-lspconfig/lsp/lua_ls.lua
    lsp/pyright.lua       -> internal/gen/corpus/nvim-lspconfig/lsp/pyright.lua
    lsp/rust_analyzer.lua -> internal/gen/corpus/nvim-lspconfig/lsp/rust_analyzer.lua
    lsp/vtsls.lua         -> internal/gen/corpus/nvim-lspconfig/lsp/vtsls.lua

The .lua files are unmodified; their sha256 digests are published in
internal/gen/corpus/nvim-lspconfig/PROVENANCE.md and re-checked by
internal/gen/corpus_test.go, so an in-place edit fails the build rather
than turning the snapshot into an unattributed fork.

Derivative work, and the changes made to produce it (Apache-2.0 section
4(b)): internal/serverdef/builtins_gen.go is generated from that snapshot
by internal/gen. It carries each server's command, filetypes-mapped-to-
language-ids and, where upstream states them declaratively, its root
markers. It does not carry upstream's Lua behaviour (root_dir, on_attach,
on_init, before_init, get_language_id), its editor policy (settings,
capabilities) or its Neovim-only filetypes; and it adds path globs,
install specs, and root markers transcribed from the Lua that computes
them upstream. Every one of those changes is recorded, per server and
per key, in the comments of builtins_gen.go itself, and the policy behind
them in internal/gen/curate.go.

Helix's languages.toml (MPL-2.0) is deliberately NOT used, and no
generator reads it: PLAN.md §9.3 flags its file-level copyleft as an
unresolved question for embedded generated data, and nvim-lspconfig's
Apache-2.0 raises no such question.

